  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "The strongest finding so far is that multiprofile aggregation (avgpool) on scvi_n200 RNA yielded a ~13-point accuracy gain (0.520→0.650, config_005), making aggregation the most impactful design axis identified. The key uncertainty is whether avgpool is near-optimal or whether a more expressive transformer aggregation can extract additional signal from the multi-profile representations. config_006 changes exactly one variable (aggregation: avgpool→transformer) relative to the current best (config_005), cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. If transformer outperforms avgpool, it reveals further headroom in the aggregation axis and justifies exploring transformer in multimodal settings later; if it does not, it confirms avgpool is sufficient and redirects the budget toward other axes (encoder choice via scgpt, or the multimodal fusion question). This is the highest-information next step because it directly extends the largest observed effect with a minimal, interpretable change, avoiding the confound of simultaneously introducing a weak image modality (config_010 showed image alone is only 0.208) before fully characterizing the RNA-side design space."
}

